v {xschem version=3.4.8RC file_version=1.2
*
* mini-MOSbius programmable PMOS current source (a 1:ratio mirror slave).
* Drawn as a current source because that is what it behaves like: the
* only current-carrying terminal is `out`, from the VAPWR end, and the
* VAPWR end is fixed.
*
* Neither the body nor `ibias` is drawn. Both are hard-wired on silicon
* (the body to a rail you cannot route; `ibias` to the chip's one bias
* reference, SPEC.md Sec 2.11) -- drawing either would only add a wire
* you are never allowed to place anywhere else. Both are supplied
* instead by the `extra` mechanism below: the netlist still gets the
* connection, the schematic does not. Override per instance with
* ibias=<net>/b=<net> if you ever need to (TODO.md Sec 2, closed
* 2026-08-22: verified wiring either to a real net routed clean with no
* warning, since the router ignored both completely).
*
*
* This symbol holds ONE transistor: the mirror slave. The reference leg
* it copies lives once per chip, in mini_mosbius.sch's bias generator,
* the same way the chip has one mirror_n reference feeding every
* programmable leg. Until 2026-08-28 every one of these symbols carried
* its own private reference diode, so N devices on a sheet split the
* chip's one reference current N ways: two mosbius_nsink at ratio=2
* measured -99 uA each where -200 uA was right.
*
* Drawn as what it is: one transistor with a fixed gate. The gate and the
* rail end are terminated, not open stubs -- they are supplied through
* `extra` and there is no pin box on either, so there is nothing to wire
* and nothing a wire could silently miss. Only the drain has a pin.
*
* The channel and gate bars are drawn longer than mosbius_nmos/mosbius_pmos
* on purpose: these are L=1 devices against those L=0.5 ones, and a longer
* channel is what makes a mirror leg a usable current source at all.
*
* It is deliberately not an ideal-current-source circle any more. This is
* a mirror leg: its current droops with output voltage (about 12 uA/V,
* ~85 kOhm) and collapses as the drain approaches its rail. A current
* source glyph promises behaviour the hardware does not have; see
* examples/currentsource/ for the measured I-V curve.
*
* The pin-box (B) record below is declared in netlist pin order, which
* is also the .subckt port order -- extra pins are appended, in the
* order `extra` lists them. mosbius/netlist.py's DEVICE_PINS holds a
* matching copy -- change both together.
}
G {}
K {type=subcircuit
format="@spiceprefix@name @pinlist @ibias @b @symname ratio=@ratio"
template="name=M1 ratio=1 ibias=ibias_p b=VAPWR spiceprefix=X"
extra="ibias b"
}
V {}
S {}
F {}
E {}
L 4 -15 -40 -15 40 {}
L 4 -15 -20 0 -20 {}
L 4 0 -30 0 -20 {}
L 4 0 -35 0 -30 {}
L 4 -12 -35 12 -35 {}
L 4 -15 20 0 20 {}
L 4 0 20 0 30 {}
L 4 0 30 0 40 {}
L 4 -25 -25 -25 25 {}
L 4 -40 0 -32.5 0 {}
B 5 -2.5 37.5 2.5 42.5 {name=out dir=inout}
A 4 -28.75 0 3.75 270 360 {}
P 4 5 -43 -3 -37 -3 -37 3 -43 3 -43 -3 {fill=true}
T {@name} 24 -17 0 0 0.2 0.2 {}
T {ratio=@ratio} 24 1 0 0 0.15 0.15 {}
T {@ibias} -95 -8 0 0 0.26 0.26 {layer=1}
T {@b} 14 -46 0 0 0.26 0.26 {layer=1}
T {@#0:net_name} 6 44 0 0 0.15 0.15 {layer=15 hide=instance}
